<translate>
<!--T:1-->
A formula on a {{SITENAME}} site is written once, while the site is being built, and what the reader gets is the writing. [<tvar name="1">https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Extension:Math</tvar> Math] is the extension for it, and unlike a [[<tvar name="2">Special:MyLanguage/Charts</tvar>|chart]] it wants nothing beside MediaWiki. It is in the image already, and naming it is the whole of the setup.

<!--T:2-->
This page writes one:
</translate>

<math display="block">\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{n^2} = \frac{\pi^2}{6}</math>

<translate>
<!--T:3-->
What the reader gets is [<tvar name="1">https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/MathML</tvar> MathML] sitting in the HTML, which a current browser draws by itself. There is no picture to fetch and no script to run, and the formula stays text: a reader can select it, and a screen reader can say it.

<!--T:4-->
== What a site declares ==
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="yaml" copy>
extensions:
  - Math
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:5-->
That is all of it. Math is [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Extensions#What is already there</tvar>|bundled with MediaWiki]], so there is no repository to name and no commit to pin.

<!--T:6-->
== How it renders ==

<!--T:7-->
Math has several rendering modes, and {{SITENAME}} takes the ones that render here:

<!--T:8-->
; <code>native</code>
: MathML, written by PHP. The default, and what the formula above is.
; <code>mathjax</code>
: The same MathML, drawn by the MathJax library in the browser. It costs every page of the site that library.
; <code>source</code>
: The LaTeX, left as it was written.

<!--T:9-->
Math's other two modes, <code>mathml</code> and <code>latexml</code>, fetch each formula from a server rather than writing it here. {{SITENAME}} does not offer them. Naming one, or an address for one, stops the build and says which line did it.

<!--T:10-->
== Writing a formula ==
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
<math>E = mc^2</math>
<math display="block">\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2}\,dx = \sqrt{\pi}</math>
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:11-->
Inline by default. <code>display="block"</code> puts the formula on a line of its own and centres it, which is what the one at the top of this page does. What a formula may contain is [<tvar name="1">https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Help:Displaying_a_formula</tvar> the LaTeX subset Math accepts], and one it cannot read stops the build rather than publishing an error message where the formula should be.
</translate>

